{"title": "Art Gallery", "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:322px;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Artgallerymain.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img src=\"/images/thumb/Artgallerymain.jpg/320px-Artgallerymain.jpg?115295\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Artgallerymain.jpg/480px-Artgallerymain.jpg?115295 1.5x, /images/thumb/Artgallerymain.jpg/640px-Artgallerymain.jpg?115295 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a>  <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Artgallerymain.jpg\" class=\"internal\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The main entrance in the Art Gallery. Note how the door has transformed into a painting.</div></div></div>\n<p>The <b>Art Gallery</b> is a museum themed interior that most commonly spawns on <a href=\"/wiki/Cubatres\" title=\"Cubatres\">Cubatres</a>. It always has three floors, and the main entrance is always on the second floor. After stepping away from main entrance the door visually transforms into a painting.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Rooms\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Rooms</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Interior_Features\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Interior Features</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Hazards\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Hazards</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#&gt;_The_Painting\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; The Painting</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Secondary_Objectives\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Secondary Objectives</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Decipher_the_Code\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Decipher the Code</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Discover_the_Tower\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Discover the Tower</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Crack_the_Vault\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Crack the Vault</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Rewards\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rewards</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Event:_Lost_Corridors\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Event: Lost Corridors</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#&gt;_Gallery\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">&gt; Gallery</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Rooms\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Rooms\">&gt; Rooms</span></h2>\n<ul><li><b>First Floor</b> - The first floor has many statues of entities, moons, and display cases. Scrap can spawn in these display cases, which can be broken by interacting with them multiple times or hitting them with a shovel.</li>\n<li><b>Second Floor</b> - The second floor is the painting gallery and scrap generally spawns on the tables or pedestals. There is an additional part of this area with a wooden floor and many statues of hoarding bugs.</li>\n<li><b>Third Floor</b> - The third floor is a more expansive wooden storage area with various boxes, statues, paintings, etc. Scrap can spawn on the floor here.</li>\n<li><b>Cube Display</b> - Several chairs lying in front of a display case with a device to input a code next to it. This room typically spawns adjacent to the main entrance and the display case holds the <a class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" href=\"#&gt;_Secondary_Objectives\"><b>Secondary Objective</b></a> reward.</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Interior_Features\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Interior_Features\">&gt; Interior Features</span></h2>\n<ul><li><b>Elevators</b> - Two elevators connect to all three floors and can be used to go between them. Music can be heard playing from the elevators when nearby to indicate their position. A player can drop down from one floor to the next and take 50 damage without using an elevator, but dropping from the third floor to the first floor deals 100 damage. Entities can travel between floors through the broken elevator shaft.</li>\n<li><b>Lasso Man Sighting</b> - Occasionally brief visions of a <b>Lasso Man</b> may appear that fades out of view after a couple seconds or upon getting close to it.</li>\n<li><b>Breaker Box</b> - The breaker box in the Art Gallery is always accompanied by the same text, and turning it off can cause some secrets to be revealed.</li>\n<li><b>Movable Painting</b> - Some paintings can be moved to reveal scrap behind them. If the <b>Breaker Box</b> is turned off, the paintings that can be moved will have a large X on them.</li>\n<li><b>Fog Machine</b> - A fog machine can be found in the interior, primarily on the second floor, and reduces visibility in the surrounding area. It can be disabled by interacting with it.</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Hazards\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Hazards\">&gt; Hazards</span></h2>\n<ul><li><b>Lasso</b> - A lasso that falls and hangs from the ceiling swaying around, dealing 666 damage to any player that walks into it and hanging them. Their corpse will be left hanging from the ceiling afterward.</li>\n<li><b>Mysterious Painting</b> - <b>Lasso Man</b> will stalk players and appear in paintings they were last around or are currently near. He starts at the back of the painting and quickly moves forward to be front and center of it, accompanied by a sound effect. If a player makes too much noise near the painting, <b>Lasso Man</b> will lash out of it with long, sweeping tendrils that deal 666 damage to players if they come into contact with the ends of them. <b>Lasso Man</b> will then shortly retreat back into the painting and disappear.</li></ul>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_The_Painting\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_The_Painting\">&gt; The Painting</span></h2>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:322px;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg/320px-ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg?a8967a\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg/480px-ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg?a8967a 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg/640px-ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg?a8967a 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a>  <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryThePainting.jpg\" class=\"internal\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>A close-up of The Painting attached to the wall after having broken its glass display case.</div></div></div>\n<p>The Painting serves as the apparatus for the interior, but it is not guaranteed to spawn. It is worth \u25ae220, is two-handed, and weighs 31lbs. It can be found in a glass casing at the end of a large room with several chairs, two Lasso Man statues, and a clock. This room always generates on the second floor.\n</p><p>When a player enters this room, an alarm will go off, sets of lasers will appear, and the clock will start ticking from 12 o'clock. A player must reach the end of the room and retrieve The Painting without being detected by the lasers and within about 90 seconds. If a player is detected or time runs out, The Painting can no longer be grabbed and will shortly be shredded. If a player successfully grabs The Painting, it will trigger all apparatus related events.\n</p><p>Players can safely stand between each set of lasers. On the left side of the room there is a note that provides instructions on how to move between the sets of lasers without being detected. When the lasers blink once, the lasers will shortly disappear and make it safe to move. When the lasers blink twice, it is not safe to move as the lasers disappear and reappear too quickly. When the lasers blink three times, it is not initially safe to move when the lasers briefly disappear but is safe to move the second time they disappear.\n</p><p>At the beginning, players can hug the wall to get to the center pathway and avoid having to deal with the chairs. Players should then get as close to each set of lasers as possible to make it easier to safely get between them. Although it can be difficult to discern between two or three blinks, it is very easy to tell when one blink happens and the timing for moving for one or three blinks is rather forgiving. Additionally, players should make sure to be checking their backs for entities, as they can come into the room.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Secondary_Objectives\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Secondary_Objectives\">&gt; Secondary Objectives</span></h2>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:322px;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg/320px-ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg?d03837\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg/480px-ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg?d03837 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg/640px-ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg?d03837 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a>  <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryCubeDisplay.jpg\" class=\"internal\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The Cube Display that holds the reward with the device to input the code next to it.</div></div></div><p>One of three unique objectives will randomly generate for players to complete for one of three valuable rewards that will spawn inside the <b>Cube Display</b>.\n</p><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Decipher_the_Code\">Decipher the Code</span></h3>\n<p>After turning off the breaker box, four symbols will appear at the bottom of the <b>Cube Display</b>. Players must wander around the <b>Second Floor</b> and find those four symbols with a number nearby. Players must then return to the <b>Cube Display</b> and input the numbered code matching the symbol code.\n</p><p>If successful, a sound effect will play and the <b>Cube Display</b> will open for players to ge their reward.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Discover_the_Tower\">Discover the Tower</span></h3>\n<p>If players turn off the breaker box, they'll receive a hint at the bottom of the <b>Cube Display</b> to find a tower. This tower is a moving pillar with several hoarding bugs on the <b>First Floor</b>. The hoarding bugs with an X on them can be interacted with to turn them around and reveal a paper attached to their back. One of the papers will have the code written on it.\n</p><p>After players learn the code, they can return to the <b>Cube Display</b>, input the code, and get their reward.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Crack_the_Vault\">Crack the Vault</span></h3>\n<p>If players turn off the breaker box, they'll receive a hint at the bottom of the <b>Cube Display</b> to find a vault. This vault spawns on the <b>Second Floor</b> in the area with wooden tiles.\n</p><p>The vault will have three small dials and one large dial on it. Players must repeatedly turn the small dials until they hear a noticeably different click sound. Once all three small dials are in place, players must look at what numbers they point to and add them together. The larger dial must then be turned to that number. For example, if the three small dials point to 5, 10, and 20 respectively, the large dial must be turned to 35. Players can then repeatedly interact with the door handle to try and open the door.\n</p><p>If successful, the door light will turn green and swing open to reveal the code. Players can then return to the <b>Cube Display</b>, input the code, and get their reward.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rewards\">Rewards</span></h3>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"text-align: center;\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<caption style=\"white-space: nowrap;\">Art Gallery Secondary Rewards\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Scrap Name</th>\n<th>Image</th>\n<th>Conductive</th>\n<th>Weight (lbs)</th>\n<th>Base Value</th>\n<th>Minimum Value</th>\n<th>Minimum Solo Value</th>\n<th>Maximum Value</th>\n<th>Maximum Solo Value\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Old idolised cube</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Old_idolised_cube.png\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Old idolised cube.png\" src=\"/images/thumb/Old_idolised_cube.png/60px-Old_idolised_cube.png?32b1c2\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"item-preview thumbborder\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Old_idolised_cube.png/90px-Old_idolised_cube.png?32b1c2 1.5x, /images/thumb/Old_idolised_cube.png/120px-Old_idolised_cube.png?32b1c2 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></div></div></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>17</td>\n<td>160</td>\n<td>160</td>\n<td>187</td>\n<td>183</td>\n<td>214\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Idolised cube</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Idolised_cube.png\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Idolised cube.png\" src=\"/images/thumb/Idolised_cube.png/60px-Idolised_cube.png?5d86ac\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"item-preview thumbborder\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Idolised_cube.png/90px-Idolised_cube.png?5d86ac 1.5x, /images/thumb/Idolised_cube.png/120px-Idolised_cube.png?5d86ac 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></div></div></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>17</td>\n<td>270</td>\n<td>270</td>\n<td>315</td>\n<td>310</td>\n<td>362\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pristine idolised cube</td>\n<td><div class=\"center\"><div class=\"floatnone\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Pristine_idolised_cube.png\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Pristine idolised cube.png\" src=\"/images/thumb/Pristine_idolised_cube.png/60px-Pristine_idolised_cube.png?74bd09\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"item-preview thumbborder\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Pristine_idolised_cube.png/90px-Pristine_idolised_cube.png?74bd09 1.5x, /images/thumb/Pristine_idolised_cube.png/120px-Pristine_idolised_cube.png?74bd09 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></div></div></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>17</td>\n<td>420</td>\n<td>420</td>\n<td>491</td>\n<td>482</td>\n<td>583\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p>The reward is randomized, but the chance for a more valuable reward is increased by how early in the day players complete the objective and is influenced by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://lethal.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics#Furniture_luck\">the vanilla luck system</a>. The value of the reward is additionally increased by a difficulty multiplier, ranging from 0.6x to 1.4x, and a solo (singleplayer) multiplier of 1.17x. <b>Discover the Tower</b> and <b>Crack the Vault</b> are considered Easy difficulty and have a 1.0x multiplier. <b>Decipher the Code</b> is considered Medium difficulty and has a 1.15x multiplier. The base value and multipliers for objective rewards can be adjusted in the Wesleys Interior Tools config under the Secondary Objectives section.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Event:_Lost_Corridors\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Event:_Lost_Corridors\">&gt; Event: Lost Corridors</span></h2>\n<div class=\"thumb tright\"><div class=\"thumbinner\" style=\"width:322px;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg/320px-ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg?96c2a0\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\" class=\"thumbimage\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg/480px-ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg?96c2a0 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg/640px-ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg?96c2a0 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a>  <div class=\"thumbcaption\"><div class=\"magnify\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryLostCorridorsEntrance.jpg\" class=\"internal\" title=\"Enlarge\"></a></div>The entrance to the Lost Corridors.</div></div></div><p>The <b>Lost Corridors</b> can generate connected to the <b>Second Floor</b>. The entrance is a door with an outline of <b>Lasso Man</b> above it.\n</p><p>Behind the door is a staircase that leads into a maze with statues of <b>Lasso Man</b>, various boxes, etc., scattered around. The general layout of the maze is always the same but what pathways are open or blocked off is random. Players must find their way through the maze to a door at the end of it. This door can be locked, but a key spawns next to it. Inside the room will be a painting with <b>Lasso Man</b> in it as well as a <b>Crystal of wicked soul</b> next to the painting.\n</p><p>As soon as a player enters the room through or near the doorway, <a href=\"/wiki/Lasso_Man\" title=\"Lasso Man\"><b>Lasso Man</b></a> will come out of the painting and spawn as an actual entity. He is a variant of the Jester that almost immediately spawns in his chasing state, but he has a significantly slower roaming speed and maximum chase speed. Players must escape back through the maze while <b>Lasso Man</b> chases them. Since <b>Lasso Man</b> is a Jester variant, he will target all players in the interior until they leave and then roam the interior looking for players for the rest of the day.\n</p><p>It is recommended to map out a specific path to escape from before entering the room and triggering <b>Lasso Man</b>, as running into a dead-end can easily result in death. Spray paint is especially useful for this. It is also currently possible but not advised to use extension ladders to both clip into and out of the room to get <b>Lasso Man</b> stuck if the door is locked, potentially even being able to avoid triggering his spawn entirely, while still obtaining the reward.\n</p><p>The <b>Crystal of wicked soul</b> is the reward for the event. It is conductive, weighs 8lbs, and is worth \u25ae196.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Gallery\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Gallery\">&gt; Gallery</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryFirstFloorHallway.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A hallway with many statues of entities on the first floor.\"><img alt=\"A hallway with many statues of entities on the first floor.\" src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryFirstFloorHallway.jpg/120px-ArtGalleryFirstFloorHallway.jpg?65e9e3\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryFirstFloorHallway.jpg/180px-ArtGalleryFirstFloorHallway.jpg?65e9e3 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGalleryFirstFloorHallway.jpg/240px-ArtGalleryFirstFloorHallway.jpg?65e9e3 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A hallway with many statues of entities on the first floor.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryMoonDisplay.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A room with moons and planets hung from the ceiling on the first floor.\"><img alt=\"A room with moons and planets hung from the ceiling on the first floor.\" src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryMoonDisplay.jpg/120px-ArtGalleryMoonDisplay.jpg?b28a2c\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryMoonDisplay.jpg/180px-ArtGalleryMoonDisplay.jpg?b28a2c 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGalleryMoonDisplay.jpg/240px-ArtGalleryMoonDisplay.jpg?b28a2c 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A room with moons and planets hung from the ceiling on the first floor.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryLeviathan.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A room with a statue of an Earth Leviathan on the first floor.\"><img alt=\"A room with a statue of an Earth Leviathan on the first floor.\" src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryLeviathan.jpg/120px-ArtGalleryLeviathan.jpg?6d29a0\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryLeviathan.jpg/180px-ArtGalleryLeviathan.jpg?6d29a0 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGalleryLeviathan.jpg/240px-ArtGalleryLeviathan.jpg?6d29a0 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A room with a statue of an Earth Leviathan on the first floor.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGallerySecondFloorWood.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"The wooden floor on the second floor.\"><img alt=\"The wooden floor on the second floor.\" src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGallerySecondFloorWood.jpg/120px-ArtGallerySecondFloorWood.jpg?f17106\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGallerySecondFloorWood.jpg/180px-ArtGallerySecondFloorWood.jpg?f17106 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGallerySecondFloorWood.jpg/240px-ArtGallerySecondFloorWood.jpg?f17106 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">The wooden floor on the second floor.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryThirdFloor.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"A single tile being generated for the third floor.\"><img alt=\"A single tile being generated for the third floor.\" src=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryThirdFloor.jpg/120px-ArtGalleryThirdFloor.jpg?4a021c\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/ArtGalleryThirdFloor.jpg/180px-ArtGalleryThirdFloor.jpg?4a021c 1.5x, /images/thumb/ArtGalleryThirdFloor.jpg/240px-ArtGalleryThirdFloor.jpg?4a021c 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">A single tile being generated for the third floor.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:ArtGalleryElevator.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"The elevators viewed from the second floor.\"><img alt=\"The elevators viewed from the s